    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="pm_d51">

                <pb facs="pm_d51-1" n="1" xml:id="pm_d51-1"/>

                <head>PM–51. Memorandum from the Director of the Executive Secretariat (Calhoun) to
                    the President’s Staff Secretary (Goodpaster)<anchor n="1" xml:id="pm_d51-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1960-08-22">August 22, 1960</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Senator Green’s Letter on Implementation of Nine Point program for
                            Panama.<anchor n="2" xml:id="pm_d51-f2"/></item>
                </list>
                <p>In accordance with your request of August 15, I am enclosing a suggested reply to
                    Senator Green for Mr. McCabe’s signature. Senator Green’s letter is returned for
                    your files.</p>
                <closer><signed><list>
                            <item><hi rendition="#bold">Walter J. Stoessel. Jr.</hi></item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#bold">John A. Calhoun</hi><anchor n="3"
                                    xml:id="pm_d51-f3"/></item>
                        </list></signed></closer>
                <pb facs="1060" n="972" type="typeset" xml:id="pg972"/>



                <xi:include href="pm_d51-a1.xml" xpointer="pm_d51-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#pm_d51-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="pm_d51-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 611.19/8–1560. Drafted by Sharp on
                    August 18.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#pm_d51-f2" n="2" xml:id="pm_d51-f2-content">
                <p>A copy of Senator Green’s letter of August 12 to the President is attached to the
                    source text, but not printed here.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#pm_d51-f3" n="3" xml:id="pm_d51-f3-content">
                <p>Walter J. Stoessel, Jr., the Deputy Director of the Executive Secretariat, signed
                    for Calhoun.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
